        }
      },
      "required": [
        "sessionId"
      ],
      "description": "`session/reopen`: stop the session's agent and take the session up again in a new process\nof the version the agent's new sessions get, through ACP `session/resume` or\n`session/load`. The session keeps its id and journal, where an `agentReopened` event marks\nthe change. While a turn runs or a request waits, it waits for them. When the new version\ncan't take the session up, the old one does again, and the event says why. Anything that\nlived only in the old process, such as its background commands, ends with it."
    },
